From 2823460f23d0a6db8cca1365ad18770b8f045c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:05:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(write): keep maxReads on createPaste after MIME
 helper split
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Context:
Replay of Patch 130 onto assembled 010–120 left POST create wiring
wrong: cherry-pick put maxReads on storedMimeTypeForUpload (Patch 070)
and omitted it from createPaste. PUT updatePaste was already correct.
Source PR #115 is not rewritten.

Expected behavior:
POST create stores maxReads and readStateVersion on paste metadata.
MIME sniff options stay filename / encryptionScheme / isMPUComplete.

Acceptance criteria:
- createPaste receives maxReads and readStateVersion
- storedMimeTypeForUpload does not take those fields
- r=1 POST still burns after the first content GET

Constraints:
- Replay-adaptation only. Do not merge into upstream-sync.

Validation:
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- 30 files / 243 tests PASS
- lint, typecheck, Prettier, frontend build, wrangler dry-run PASS

Docs:
- N/A (wiring only)

Refs:
- Issue #84
- Source PR #115 HEAD 7540a3cad785404463cab71a071deebad50081b7
- Patch ID 130-max-reads-consume

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts b/worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts
index 6b5cb3229314e33c0282f362d4932dbf755a9767..e0632d3a9af6be010b6b935625cebe3525ceb6db 100644
--- a/worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts
+++ b/worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts
@@ -294,8 +294,6 @@ export async function handlePostOrPut(
       filename: storedFilename,
       encryptionScheme,
       isMPUComplete,
-      maxReads,
-      readStateVersion,
     })
     try {
       const newMetadata = await createPaste(env, pasteName, content, {
@@ -309,6 +307,8 @@ export async function handlePostOrPut(
         encryptionScheme,
         mimeType,
         isMPUComplete: isMPUComplete || namedR2Object !== undefined,
+        maxReads,
+        readStateVersion,
       })
 
       return makeResponse(
-- 
